Added optional capture of the network traffic PEAT sends and receives during ``scan``, ``pull`` and ``push`` to a PCAP file in the run directory (``pcaps/``), using tcpdump or Scapy's ``AsyncSniffer``. Enable it with ``--capture-traffic`` (``--pcap``) or ``capture_traffic: true``, and tune it with ``--capture-interfaces``, ``--capture-filter`` and ``--capture-tool``. Capture failures (e.g. missing privileges, Npcap or tcpdump) log a warning and never fail the run. The M340 module now also saves the UMAS packets of a project download as ``umas-packets.pcapng``, a reconstructed TCP/Modbus session annotated with UMAS function names that can be opened in Wireshark, even if the download fails partway (disable with the ``m340.save_umas_pcap`` device option).
